WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.119
Apollo Q Labs. Level three: Risk and Volatility.

2
00:00:05.419 --> 00:00:18.412
The Greeks, measures of how an option reacts, time decay, the loss of value as time passes, I V crush, a sharp drop in I V after an event, which lowers option prices, assignment, and model limits.

3
00:00:18.412 --> 00:00:25.944
Module one: Delta and gamma. How an option's price reacts to the stock moving, and how fast that changes.

4
00:00:25.944 --> 00:00:35.396
Module two: Theta, vega, rho and I V crush. Time decay, volatility, how much prices swing, interest rates, and I V after big events.

5
00:00:35.396 --> 00:00:47.344
Module three: Assignment, expiration and pin risk. What can happen to options you sold near expiration: being made to buy or sell shares, or not knowing if you will be.

6
00:00:47.344 --> 00:00:57.564
Module four: Liquidity, big risks and model limits. Fill prices, the price your order actually gets, unlimited-risk positions, and what any model can't see.

7
00:00:57.864 --> 00:00:59.764
Start with module one.
